1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,850
What if sending NIM wasn't something that

2
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:05,510
happened after the game, but was actually

3
00:00:05,510 --> 00:00:07,320
part of the game itself?

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,720
That's the idea behind NIM Relay.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:13,640
We turned a real one-NIM transfer into a baton

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,360
that moves from runner to runner.

7
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:19,010
You receive it, carry it through your relay leg,

8
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:22,360
and pass it forward to another person.

9
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:24,320
Every runner becomes part of

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,760
the baton's history.

11
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,300
Your run is verified by our server,

12
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,160
your journey stays attached to the relay,

13
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:34,570
and the next person continues from where you left off.

14
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:37,920
And the world view lets you follow that journey

15
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:41,450
as it grows, instead of treating each game

16
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:42,960
as an isolated run.

17
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,860
Here, I'm choosing the baton's next

18
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:47,580
route and its next runner.

19
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:51,090
Then I throw it forward and approve the actual

20
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:54,460
one-NIM transfer inside Nimiq Pay.

21
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,920
And this is the part I really wanted

22
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:58,660
the product to make visible.

23
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:00,350
On the left, the sender gets

24
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:01,510
the confirmed handoff.

25
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:03,210
On the right, the next runner

26
00:01:03,210 --> 00:01:04,480
receives the baton.

27
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:07,540
There's no fake baton changing

28
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:08,720
hands in our database.

29
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,720
A real NIM transfer moves between the two wallets,

30
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,560
while NIM Relay records the verified handoff

31
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,640
and extends the journey.

32
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:19,510
The new runner can then complete their own

33
00:01:19,510 --> 00:01:21,280
leg and send it forward again.

34
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,760
Here, that same relay comes back,

35
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:25,440
creating the third verified handoff in the chain.

36
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:28,760
That loop is what everything else in NIM Relay is

37
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,010
built around: people, runs, routes,

38
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:36,480
handoffs, and a baton whose story gets longer every

39
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,670
time somebody keeps it moving.

40
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:41,100
And every handoff can be checked.

41
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,850
These are the actual mainnet transactions

42
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:46,840
behind this relay, with the one-NIM transfers

43
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,510
verified onchain.

44
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:51,460
We wanted blockchain to be something

45
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:52,770
you feel through the experience,

46
00:01:52,770 --> 00:01:54,440
not something bolted onto it.

47
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:57,040
One NIM. One relay. One journey.

48
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:59,417
How far can we keep it moving?
